---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Sandy Foley and the practical AI focus behind So you wanna... with AI."
>
  <section class="container about">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>The next chapter of practical technical blogging</h1>
    <div class="copy">
      <p>
        I previously blogged about Sitecore and Solr, with a focus on the practical details that
        matter when teams are building and maintaining real platforms.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>So you wanna... with AI</strong> continues that habit. The focus here is not AI hype
        or model-building theory. It is a working notebook on applying AI to software delivery:
        Codex workflows, prompt strategy, in-app browser usage, context management, and architecture
        judgment for .NET teams.
      </p>
      <p>
        The goal is to capture lessons that help experienced developers use AI as a serious tool
        inside existing engineering constraints.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    padding: 5rem 0;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 880px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 4.6rem);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .copy {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    color: #2f3a45;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
  }
</style>
